00:00:00.030 --> 00:00:01.330 align:start position:0%
 
in India the number of confirmed  coronavirus infections has now topped  600,000 but the Indian government is  striking back of critics who say it  hasn't done enough to fight the pandemic  it has introduced a revamped strategy to  curb the spread of the virus DWS Munir  Chaudhary brings us this report from the  worst-hit City Delhi a massive  door-to-door survey exercise has been  launched in Delhi for its entire  population of about 20 million residents  the state government is aiming to record  the health details of each and every  household to deal with the spread of  coronavirus the move has come after  weeks of scrambling for measures by both  the state and the national government to  avoid a major healthcare disaster in the  capital city which has now become the  worst hit in the country even the  government is not you know sure what  will work out and what will not work out  so I'm little scared but we can't lose  earlier we could step out a little at  least to buy essentials and groceries  but now we're worried that if we step  out at all we may get infected as part  of its revamped strategy to handle the  spread of cases the Delhi government is  taking a range of measures they include  increased testing and contact tracing  antibody testing developing a plasma  bank and providing oximeters to Corbitt  patients the government simultaneously  is trying to wrap up its healthcare  infrastructure the daily testing for  Corbett 19 has increased significantly  the state government says that it is now  conducting 20000 tests every day  apart from plans to start rapid antigen  testing which allows for faster  diagnosis of samples regular testing  camps are also being set up  especially in coronavirus hotspots known  as containment zones Sangam Behar one of  Delhi's largest and most crowded  informal settlements has several  containment zones the new testing camps  there have already started making a  difference during the past week testing  has increased many positive cases are  getting detected earlier the testing  wasn't so regular now it's daily  some 200 people are tested at each camp  here daily anybody testing positive is  immediately taken to makeshift  quarantine centers crucial for those  we're home isolation is not an option  the Delhi government has projected that  the number of cases in the capital may  rise up to half a million by the end of  July to handle such a case load some  spacious venues in the city are also  being converted into Corbett care  facilities this ashram is being prepared  to become one of the world's largest  Corbett care centers essentially an  isolation facility it has a capacity of  10,000 beds most of which are made of  prefabricated cardboard material once  opened it will provide round-the-clock  medical supervision for mild and  moderate cases there is pressure on the  general care healthcare system it is a  new disease one that we were not fully  equipped to deal with when it began and  it became a pandemic and we have to  supplement the general health care  systems even though lockdown  restrictions have been eased to some  extent in Delhi there is still much  confusion and anxiety amongst its  residents as the capital continues to  formulate and implement new strategies  it has a tough task ahead of itself as  the challenge of coronavirus has now  turned into a crisis and let's get more  I am joined now by our correspondent in  Delhi Munira Chow Deary who submitted  that report for us you looked at these  measures taken by the government in  order to contain the virus yet we're  seeing a spike in daily cases does it  mean the measures have failed well one  big reason that the spike in the number  of cases we is being attributed to if  the relaxation in the lockdown rules the  life is returning back to normalcy a lot  of economic activities have resumed  markets have opened up and Delhi being a  very densely populated city this kind of  transmission when a lot of people do  resume their daily work is quite  possible but on another side of the  story is also that after this became  evident that Delhi is seeing a lot of  cases the test  increase now jelly is testing a lot more  than a lot of other cities which are  still testing around seven or eight  thousand people per day Delhi is now  testing twenty thousand about so because  of this increased testing more and more  cases are being detected now so we are  seeing a lot of numbers coming forward  because of increased testing as well are  those tests easily accessible to  everyone who needs them who wants them  well now the testing facilities have  increased you can go and get tested in  hospitals and the bottle trees but you  do need to be sure about your symptoms  you do need a doctor's prescription  because at the moment only high risk  category people and people who are  showing certain symptoms are being  encouraged to go and get tested and in  of the containment areas as we saw in my  report in informal settlements which are  crowded the government is organizing  these regular testing camps where about  100 or 200 people are getting tested  every day and the test being used are  rapid antigen tests which are showing  results in about 15 to 20 minutes so  positive cases are quickly being either  put in isolation in home or taken to  quarantine centers tell us a little bit  more about those containment areas that  you reported on for the infected what is  what is the state of social stigma  surrounding that do people feel  stigmatized if they feel comfortable  going there well the definition of term  containment zone has been tweet a little  in the past couple of months but  essentially means an area where cases  have been detected and it's for the  government it's important to demarcate  these areas because to map local  transmission and to even prevent local  transmission so movement is restricted  not those many activities are allowed as  in other areas and people do understand  the importance of these zones but people  who do feel a little stigma are those  you know are outside whose homes for and  trying posters are being pasted those  who are coming out positive in commit  and what being put under home isolation  so certain posters are being put outside  their homes which basically declared to  what time they're supposed to be in  quarantine they feel a little stigma  coming from there but the government  feels these posters are important  because it gives them a sense of urgency  and responsibility  many are Chowdhury in telly thank you

